  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2025-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(i(i-1) = i^2 - i = -1 - i,\\) and \\((i-2)(i-3) = i^2 - 5i + 6\\) \\(= 5 - 5i.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{gathered} (-1-i)(5-5i) = -5 \\\\ {}+ 5i - 5i \\\\ {}+ 5i^2 \\\\ = -5 - 5 = -10. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Multiply in pairs: \\(i(i-1)\\) and \\((i-2)(i-3)\\)",
        "Use \\(i^2 = -1\\) to reduce each product before multiplying the two results"
      ],
